{'symbol': 'WFC', 'date': '2019-10-15 10:30:00', 'title': 'Wells Fargo & Co Reports Qtrly EPS of $0.92', 'text': 'QTRLY DILUTED EPS OF $0.92.QTRLY REVENUE OF $22.0 BILLION, UP FROM $21.9 BILLION.QTRLY DILUTED EPS OF $0.92 INCLUDED THE IMPACT OF A DISCRETE LITIGATION ACCRUAL OF LOSS OF $0.35 PER SHARE.QTRLY NET INTEREST INCOME OF $11.6 BILLION, DOWN $947 MILLION.QTRLY DILUTED EPS OF $0.92 INCLUDED A GAIN ON THE SALE OF OUR INSTITUTIONAL RETIREMENT AND TRUST BUSINESS OF $0.20 PER SHARE.QTRLY NET INTEREST MARGIN WAS 2.66%, DOWN 16 BASIS POINTS FROM THE PRIOR QUARTER.QTRLY NONINTEREST EXPENSE OF $15.2 BILLION, UP $1.4 BILLION.QTRLY NET CHARGE-OFFS OF 0.27% OF AVERAGE LOANS (ANNUALIZED), DOWN FROM 0.29%.QTRLY MORTGAGE BANKING INCOME WAS $466 MILLION, DOWN FROM $758 MILLION IN SECOND QUARTER 2019.QTRLY AVERAGE LOANS OF $949.8 BILLION, UP $10.3 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.15, REVENUE VIEW $21.19 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RESIDENTIAL HELD-FOR-SALE MORTGAGE LOAN ORIGINATIONS INCREASED IN THE THIRD QUARTER TO $38 BILLION FROM $33 BILLION IN Q2.RETURN ON EQUITY OF 9% AT QUARTER-END VERSUS 12.04% REPORTED LAST YEAR.WELLS FARGO CFO JOHN SHREWSBERRY - IN QUARTER, "BUSINESS FUNDAMENTALS WERE STRONG AS BOTH LOANS & DEPOSITS GREW FROM THE SECOND QUARTER & FROM A YEAR AGO".EFFICIENCY RATIO WAS 69.1% IN Q3 2019 VERSUS 62.3% IN Q2.QTRLY NONPERFORMING ASSETS DECREASED $317 MILLION, OR 5%, FROM SECOND QUARTER 2019 TO $6.0 BILLION.COMPANY\'S COMMON EQUITY TIER 1 RATIO (FULLY PHASED-IN) WAS 11.6% AT QUARTER-END.'}
